From 746edddaa5e3e04d591f9ad008535f0e403a321c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena <arena@local>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 12:02:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: add SM6225 SoC and Xiaomi topaz board (S1
 minimal)

First upstream-style device tree slice for SM6225 (Khaje) on this
base: CPUs/PSCI/timer/GIC, khaje GCC + RPMCC, TLMM, the QUPv3 debug
UART (serial0), Bengal interconnects and the SMD-RPM CX/MX level
votes, modelled on sm6115.dtsi. All addresses, IRQs, capacities and
the board reserved-memory map come from the live FDT of a topaz unit
and the downstream khaje/bengal DTS import, translated to the
bindings this series provides.

The board file describes memory (4 GB unit banks; the bootloader
rewrites them per SKU) and reserved-memory including the ramoops
region at 0x5d000000 the stock kernel uses, so pstore can serve as
the log channel for a future first boot without UART hardware.

Also register the SoC/board compatibles this needs: qcom,sm6225 in
arm/qcom.yaml and the UBWC table (same data as qcom,khaje),
qcom,rpm-sm6225 (binding + SMD RPM driver), qcom,sm6225-rpm-proc
and qcom,sm6225-apcs-hmss-global.

Deliberately not in this slice (later slices of the DT plan): UFS,
display, audio/ADSP, PMIC SPMI rails beyond CX/MX, cpufreq-hw/OPPs,
CPU idle states and the apps SMMU. Not boot-tested: CI dtbs/
dtbs_check only.
---
